ui.utilitycraft:info.arcane_enchanter=Enchants one item at a time. Every applied enchantment costs 12 Lapis Lazuli and 300 mB of XP. Enchantability Modules increase selection strength; the reusable Curse Protection Module prevents curses from entering the generated plan. Speed, Energy, and Hyper Processing upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Item Input§r accepts the target item.\n§bLapis Input§r accepts Lapis Lazuli.\n§1Enchantability Module§r raises enchantment strength.\n§3Curse Protection§r filters curses.\n§cOutput§r exposes the enchanted item.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9XP Input§r fills the internal XP tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.arcane_enchanter.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Item Input\n§r- §3Input All\n§r- §bLapis Input\n§r- §1Module Input\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.arcane_enchanter.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9XP Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.disenchanter=Processes one enchanted item in two selectable modes.\n\nExtraction: removes one enchantment, consumes one normal Book, and places the enchanted Book in the 4x3 output grid while leaving the updated source in its large shared slot.\nAbsorption: removes every enchantment and stores the recovered value as XP fluid.\n\nSpeed, Energy, and Hyper Processing upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Source Input§r inserts or extracts the enchanted item.\n§bBook Input§r inserts normal Books.\n§cEnchanted Books§r exposes all twelve book outputs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§cXP Output§r drains recovered XP.
ui.utilitycraft:io.disenchanter.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Source Input\n§r- §3Input All\n§r- §cOutput All\n§r- §bBook Input\n§r- §cProcessed Item\n§r- §cEnchanted Book
ui.utilitycraft:io.disenchanter.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cXP Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.industrial_crucible=Processes supported materials while generating Lava. Its six inputs form a 2x3 pooled grid and solid results use a 2x3 output grid. Cobblestone becomes Stone, Sand becomes Glass, and Clay Balls become Bricks. Processing pauses when the solid buffer or Lava tank is full. Speed, Energy, Hyper Processing, and Process Batch upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input Grid§r exposes all six material slots.\n§cOutput Grid§r exposes all six result slots.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§cLava Output§r exposes the generated Lava tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_crucible.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input Grid\n§r- §cOutput Grid
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_crucible.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cLava Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryofluid_synthesizer=Combines 4 Titanium points, 8 Lapis points, and 1,000 mB Water into 1,000 mB Cryofluid for 6,000 DE. Both resource groups accept their smaller forms, blocks, and every compressed block tier at their crafting-equivalent values. Speed, Energy, Hyper Processing, and Process Batch upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Titanium Input§r exposes four weighted input slots.\n§bLapis Input§r exposes four weighted input slots.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Water Input§r fills the Water tank.\n§cCryofluid Output§r drains the Cryofluid tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryofluid_synthesizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Titanium Input\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §bLapis Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryofluid_synthesizer.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Water Input\n§r- §cCryofluid Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryo_stabilizer=Consumes Cryofluid to stabilize up to four materials simultaneously. Each of the four input lanes writes to its paired output. Capsule insertion, capsule return, and the obsolete unstable-material guide were removed; Cryofluid enters through liquid I/O. Speed, Energy, Hyper Processing, and Process Batch upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Material Inputs§r expose the four independent lanes.\n§cStabilized Outputs§r expose all four paired results.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Cryofluid Input§r fills the internal tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_stabilizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Material Inputs\n§r- §cStabilized Outputs
ui.utilitycraft:io.arc_press_forge.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.impact_crusher.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_stabilizer.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Cryofluid Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryo_chamber=Runs three Cryo systems simultaneously. The Stabilizer converts unstable materials with Cryofluid, the frozen 3x3 grid cools complete stacks, and the generator converts Water, Titanium, and Lapis into Cryofluid. The generator accepts smaller, block, and compressed forms through direct recipes scaled from their crafting values.\n\nThe Water and Cryofluid tanks are independent. Speed and Energy upgrades affect the complete machine; Process Batch applies to the Stabilizer and Generator.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Stabilizer Input\n§bCooling Grid\n§bTitanium Input\n§9Lapis Input\n§3Input All\n§cStabilized Output\n§cCooling Grid Output\n§cOutput All\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Water Input\n§cCryofluid Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_chamber.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Stabilizer Input\n§r- §3Input All\n§r- §cOutput All\n§r- §bCooling Grid\n§r- §bTitanium Input\n§r- §9Lapis Input\n§r- §cStabilized Output\n§r- §cCooling Grid Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_chamber.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Water Input\n§r- §cCryofluid Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.cryo_freezer=Freezes up to fifteen stacks simultaneously. Place supported items anywhere in the frozen grid; completed results replace their original stacks in the same slots.\n\nRecipes use direct indexed lookup. The shared coolant tank accepts the liquid required by the active recipe, while all lanes share one energy budget.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Freezer Grid Input\n§cFreezer Grid Output\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Coolant Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_freezer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Freezer Grid Input\n§r- §cFreezer Grid Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.cryo_freezer.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Coolant Input
tile.utilitycraft:cryofluid_synthesizer.name=Cryofluid Synthesizer\n§9Superior Cryo Synthesis Branch\n§7Accepts upgrades:\n  §a§r, §b§r, §d§r, §6§r\n§o§9@UC: Ascendant Technology
entity.utilitycraft:cryofluid_synthesizer.name=Cryofluid Synthesizer
ui.utilitycraft:info.vaporworks_processor=Converts liquid inputs into pressurized Steam gas. Water produces Steam at a 1:1 ratio; Cryofluid takes longer and produces 50% more Steam. The liquid input tank and Steam gas tank each store 64,000 units.\n\nFilled Water or Cryofluid containers go in the upper-left slot and their empty containers leave below it. Empty gas capsules go in the upper-right slot; a filled 8,000-unit Steam Capsule leaves below it.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Liquid Container Input§r and §bGas Container Input§r accept containers.\n§cContainer Return§r and §cSteam Container Output§r expose processed containers.\n§9Input All§r and §cOutput All§r expose both pairs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Liquid Input§r accepts Water or Cryofluid.\n\nGas I/O:\n§cSteam Output§r exposes the Steam tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.vaporworks_processor.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Liquid Container Input\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cOutput All\n§r- §bGas Container Input\n§r- §cContainer Return\n§r- §cSteam Container Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.vaporworks_processor.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Liquid Input
ui.utilitycraft:io.vaporworks_processor.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cSteam Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.energizer=Converts supported iron materials into energized components. Place materials in either input; the Primary channel is checked first, then Auxiliary. Each recipe defines its own processing time and total energy cost.\n\nBoth channels resolve recipes through direct indexed lookup. Speed and Energy upgrades affect processing, while Process Batch controls how many items complete per paid cycle.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Primary Input§r exposes the first-priority channel.\n§bAuxiliary Input§r exposes the fallback channel.\n§9Input All§r exposes both inputs.\n§cOutput§r exposes the result slot.
ui.utilitycraft:io.energizer.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Primary Input\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §bAuxiliary Input\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:info.catalyst_weaver=Combines one base item with an exact set of up to six catalysts. Catalyst positions do not matter, but extra catalyst types prevent a match. Some recipes also consume Lava, Liquified Aetherium, or Dark Matter from the internal 128,000 mB tank.\n\nCatalyst Weaver recipes and registered UtilityCraft Infuser recipes are indexed when loaded. Recipe lookup does not scan the complete registry while machines run.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Base Input§r exposes the base item.\n§bCatalyst 1§r, §1Catalyst 2§r, §bCatalyst 3§r, §9Catalyst 4§r, §bCatalyst 5§r, and §1Catalyst 6§r each expose one catalyst slot.\n§3All Catalysts§r exposes all six catalyst slots.\n§cMain Output§r and §cResidue Output§r expose their respective results.\n§cOutput All§r exposes both outputs.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§9Catalyst Fluid Input§r exposes the internal tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.catalyst_weaver.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Base Input\n§r- §3All Catalysts\n§r- §cOutput All\n§r- §bCatalyst 1\n§r- §1Catalyst 2\n§r- §bCatalyst 3\n§r- §9Catalyst 4\n§r- §bCatalyst 5\n§r- §1Catalyst 6\n§r- §cMain Output\n§r- §cResidue Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.catalyst_weaver.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Catalyst Fluid Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.liquifier=Converts supported solid materials into Liquified Aetherium or Dark Matter. Insert the solid material on the left; produced liquid accumulates in the output tank on the right. Some recipes can also create an optional solid residue.\n\nThe tank accepts one liquid type at a time and stores up to 640,000 mB. Drain it before switching between Liquified Aetherium and Dark Matter. The liquid can be extracted through liquid I/O or standard UtilityCraft fluid containers.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the solid material input.\n§cResidue Output§r exposes the optional byproduct.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§cLiquid Output§r exposes the produced liquid tank.
ui.utilitycraft:io.liquifier.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cResidue Output
ui.utilitycraft:io.liquifier.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §cLiquid Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.residue_processor=Recovers materials from residue, dead coral, terracotta and organic blocks. Open Recipes to view inputs, all four possible outputs, quantities and chances. The upper-left slot holds the primary result; the other three hold secondary products. Processing waits when a required output slot is full. Item I/O: Primary Output selects the first slot, Residue Output selects the three secondary slots, and Output All selects all four.
ui.utilitycraft:io.residue_processor.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cOutput All\n§r- §cPrimary Output\n§r- §cResidue Output
ui.utilitycraft:info.centrifugal_siever=Processes UtilityCraft sieve recipes through a shared four-slot input pool and a reusable Mesh. Drops are rolled once per processed item and stored in the 15-slot output buffer.\n\nSteam is optional. A boosted cycle consumes 125 units per processed item, runs at 150% rate, and costs 125% energy.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes all material inputs.\n§bMesh§r exposes the mesh slot.\n§cOutput§r exposes the output buffer.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.
ui.utilitycraft:io.centrifugal_siever.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §bMesh\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.centrifugal_siever.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.dual_siever=Runs two UtilityCraft sieve lanes against one shared 20-slot output buffer. Each lane has one material input and its own reusable Mesh.\n\nIND: each ready lane advances and completes independently.\nSHR: both lanes advance together only when both are ready and contain the same input item.\n\nSteam is optional. A boosted lane consumes 125 units per item, runs at 150% rate, and costs 125% energy. Speed, Energy, Hyper Processing, and Process Batch upgrades are accepted.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Lane A§r and §bLane B§r expose their inputs and meshes.\n§cOutput§r exposes the shared buffer.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.
ui.utilitycraft:io.dual_siever.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Lane A Input\n§r- §9All Inputs\n§r- §bAll Meshes\n§r- §bLane A Mesh\n§r- §9Lane B Input\n§r- §bLane B Mesh\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:io.dual_siever.gases=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Steam Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.impact_crusher=Processes two Crusher recipes in parallel into a shared 4x2 output area. Lava heats the machine and fuels each craft; processing begins after the minimum operating temperature is reached. Steam actively dissipates heat. At maximum heat, Thermal Lock stops all processing for at least 30 seconds and releases only after the machine cools below its operating threshold.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input 1§r and §bInput 2§r feed the two lanes.\n§cOutputs§r expose all eight result slots.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§vFuel Input§r accepts Lava.\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam for cooling.
ui.utilitycraft:io.impact_crusher.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input 1\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §bInput 2\n§r- §cOutput 1\n§r- §cOutput 2\n§r- §cOutput 3
ui.utilitycraft:io.impact_crusher.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §vLava Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.industrial_burner=Processes three Furnace recipes in parallel. Each lane has one input, one progress bar, and a dedicated 2x1 output buffer. Lava can add up to one bonus craft per base craft, consuming 250 mB for each bonus craft.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Inputs 1-3§r feed their respective lanes.\n§cOutputs 1-3§r each expose two slots.\n§cOutput All§r exposes all six result slots.\n\nLiquid I/O:\n§vFuel Input§r accepts Lava.
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_burner.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input 1\n§r- §9Input All\n§r- §cOutput All\n§r- §bInput 2\n§r- §9Input 3\n§r- §cOutput 1\n§r- §cOutput 2\n§r- §cOutput 3
ui.utilitycraft:io.industrial_burner.liquids=I/O Modes:\n§r- §vFuel Input
ui.utilitycraft:info.arc_press_forge=Processes Electro Press recipes through shared 2x2 input and output buffers.\n\nLow Loss: preserves every output at the normal superior rate.\nHigh Speed: doubles processing rate and batch size, but each completed batch has a 50% chance to lose one output.\n\nSteam optionally adds a further 150% rate boost for 125 units per craft at 125% energy cost.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the complete input grid.\n§cOutput§r exposes the complete output grid.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.
ui.utilitycraft:io.arc_press_forge.items=I/O Modes:\n§r- §9Input\n§r- §cOutput
ui.utilitycraft:info.pulverizer=Processes Crusher recipes through shared 2x2 input and output buffers. All four input slots form one pool, and all four output slots form another.\n\nThe machine runs normally without Steam. When Steam is available, each craft consumes 250 units, processing rate increases to 175%, and energy cost increases to 150%.\n\nItem I/O:\n§9Input§r exposes the complete input grid.\n§cOutput§r exposes the complete output grid.\n\nGas I/O:\n§9Steam Input§r accepts Steam.

